WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:04.760
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

2
00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:06.080
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

3
00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:07.360
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》。

4
00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:08.600
And we're best friends.
我们也是最好的朋友。

5
00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:12.420
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.
现在，我们专门为你们制作了《办公室》终极重温播客。

6
00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:19.400
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
每周，我们都会剖析一集《办公室》，并分享只有身临其境的我们两人才能告诉你的独家幕后故事。

7
00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:20.540
We're The Office Ladies.
我们是《办公室》女士。

8
00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:25.890
Hi there, everybody.
大家好。

9
00:00:26.870 --> 00:00:32.470
All right, today we're going to talk about counseling, which is Season 7, Episode 2.
好了，今天我们要聊的是《咨询》，也就是第七季第二集。

10
00:00:33.310 --> 00:00:41.710
But first, Ange, I feel like I want to share with our podcast listeners the morning that we had getting here.
但在开始之前，安吉，我觉得我想和我们的播客听众分享一下我们今天早上来这里的经历。

11
00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:42.350
Okay.
好的。

12
00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:47.090
We had quite the text thread going this morning.
我们今天早上发了一长串短信。

13
00:00:47.210 --> 00:00:48.230
It was real wonky.
真是乱七八糟的。

14
00:00:48.430 --> 00:00:49.890
With Sam and Cassie, you and me.
有山姆、卡西，还有你和我。

15
00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:51.210
I've got a summer cold.
我得了夏季感冒。

16
00:00:51.370 --> 00:00:51.610
Yeah.
是啊。

17
00:00:51.770 --> 00:00:54.770
I can't believe I am congested again.
真不敢相信我又鼻塞了。

18
00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:55.870
Like, I can't believe it.
真的，我简直不敢相信。

19
00:00:55.870 --> 00:00:56.870
You just kicked it.
你才刚痊愈。

20
00:00:57.050 --> 00:00:58.730
I barely kicked it.
我还没完全好呢。

21
00:00:58.830 --> 00:00:59.710
And now it's back.
结果现在又复发了。

22
00:00:59.710 --> 00:01:03.450
This is, you know, kids going to camps, and I don't know.
你知道的，孩子们去参加夏令营，我也不知道怎么回事。

23
00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:05.270
We're bringing all the stuff home.
我们把各种病菌都带回家了。

24
00:01:05.370 --> 00:01:06.310
Jeremy McDerMs.
杰里米·麦克德姆斯。

25
00:01:06.810 --> 00:01:09.110
So this morning, y'all were checking in with me.
所以今天早上，你们都在关心我。

26
00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:10.950
You're like, Jenna, are you okay to record?
你们问，珍娜，你还能录音吗？

27
00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:13.110
And I was like, I'm going to rally.
我说，我会振作起来的。

28
00:01:13.330 --> 00:01:14.070
I'm going to do it.
我能行。

29
00:01:14.210 --> 00:01:14.350
Yeah.
没错。

30
00:01:14.530 --> 00:01:16.270
And then Sam was like.
然后山姆说。

31
00:01:16.390 --> 00:01:18.530
Yeah, I was like, I don't bring enough to this podcaSt.
是啊，我说，我为这个播客贡献得不够多。

32
00:01:18.530 --> 00:01:19.970
I'm going to bring Food Boys name.
我要带上“食物男孩”的名字。

33
00:01:20.290 --> 00:01:21.190
Aw, Sam.
噢，山姆。

34
00:01:22.050 --> 00:01:24.850
And, you know, Cassie and I are looking pretty good this morning.
而且，你知道，卡西和我今天早上看起来状态不错。

35
00:01:25.230 --> 00:01:26.150
Yeah, I don't appreciate that.
是啊，我可不这么认为。

36
00:01:26.150 --> 00:01:28.730
We both just finished off the donut.
我们俩刚吃完甜甜圈。

37
00:01:29.930 --> 00:01:31.750
Oh, yeah, they have donuts in the lobby today.
噢，对，大厅今天有甜甜圈。

38
00:01:31.930 --> 00:01:34.150
I want to point out, Jenna's almost horizontal.
我想指出的是，珍娜现在几乎是横躺着的。

39
00:01:34.350 --> 00:01:35.510
She's almost reclined.
她几乎是半躺在椅子上。

40
00:01:36.610 --> 00:01:40.790
She's pulled another chair next to her chair so she can recline.
她在自己的椅子旁边又拉了一把椅子，好让自己能躺下。

41
00:01:41.290 --> 00:01:42.270
But listen to this.
但听听这个。

42
00:01:42.430 --> 00:01:45.290
So after Sam and I are both like, we're going to do it.
在山姆和我达成一致说我们要坚持住之后。

43
00:01:45.370 --> 00:01:46.030
We're going to rally.
我们要振作起来。

44
00:01:46.250 --> 00:01:46.810
We got it.
我们能行。

45
00:01:47.410 --> 00:01:50.470
I reached into my closet to grab my office lady's hoodie,
我伸手去衣柜拿我的《办公室》女士连帽衫，

46
00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:55.310
and I sliced my finger open on a broken edge of my plastic hanger.
结果被塑料衣架的破损边缘划破了手指。

47
00:01:56.030 --> 00:01:57.170
So then I'm like, you know what?
当时我就想，你知道吗？

48
00:01:57.250 --> 00:01:58.030
It's still okay.
没关系。

49
00:01:58.030 --> 00:01:59.450
I'm still going in.
我还是要坚持去录音。

50
00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:06.330
So I'm driving in to work and driving my daughter to camp firSt.
所以我开车去上班，先送我女儿去夏令营。

51
00:02:06.830 --> 00:02:13.510
And there was this big sort of that moment where someone cut in front of the line of cars
当时有那么一瞬间，有辆车突然插到了车队前面，

52
00:02:13.510 --> 00:02:15.770
that were headed toward this one exit.
大家都正往同一个出口开去。

53
00:02:16.690 --> 00:02:19.810
Everything slowed down, and I had to slam on the brakes.
车速全慢了下来，我不得不猛踩刹车。

54
00:02:20.730 --> 00:02:27.410
But I could tell around me that, like, there was not enough space for everybody.
但我能感觉到周围的情况，就像是，空间根本不够大家挤的。

55
00:02:27.690 --> 00:02:28.390
Oh, no.
噢，不。

56
00:02:28.670 --> 00:02:29.530
Did you get hit?
你被撞了吗？

57
00:02:29.710 --> 00:02:29.970
Yeah.
是的。

58
00:02:30.130 --> 00:02:30.830
Did you hear the noise?
你听到撞击声了吗？

59
00:02:30.930 --> 00:02:31.650
You got hit?
你被撞了？

60
00:02:31.850 --> 00:02:33.190
Did the brake noise before it?
在那之前有听到刹车声吗？

61
00:02:33.530 --> 00:02:34.290
Like, were you know what's going on?
就是，你知道发生了什么吗？

62
00:02:34.330 --> 00:02:35.610
No, it wasn't that.
不，不是那样的。

63
00:02:35.610 --> 00:02:38.970
I just could feel, like, the time and space around me.
我只是能感觉到，周围的时间和空间感。

64
00:02:38.970 --> 00:02:44.590
And I said out loud to my daughter, I said, I think we're going to be in an accident.
我大声对女儿说，我说，我觉得我们要出车祸了。

65
00:02:44.850 --> 00:02:47.090
And then the person behind us ran into us.
然后后面那个人就撞上了我们。

66
00:02:47.290 --> 00:02:49.950
It was a fender bender to call it an accident.
说它是车祸，其实也就是个小刮蹭。

67
00:02:50.230 --> 00:02:51.230
It's not really an accident.
算不上真正的事故。

68
00:02:51.230 --> 00:02:56.430
And then, of course, it's L.A., so I'm expecting this person is going to take off.
当然了，毕竟是在洛杉矶，所以我以为那个人会直接逃逸。

69
00:02:56.870 --> 00:02:58.870
But I'm like, no way he's pulling over.
但我心想，他不可能靠边停车的。

70
00:02:59.150 --> 00:02:59.510
Yeah.
是啊。

71
00:02:59.510 --> 00:03:00.470
He pulled over.
他靠边停了。

72
00:03:00.750 --> 00:03:01.150
Aw.
噢。

73
00:03:01.370 --> 00:03:02.890
He gets out of his car.
他从车里走出来。

74
00:03:03.430 --> 00:03:04.250
Young guy.
是个小伙子。

75
00:03:04.410 --> 00:03:04.670
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

76
00:03:04.770 --> 00:03:05.410
So sweet.
人特别好。

77
00:03:05.590 --> 00:03:07.590
He's wearing a Vote for Pedro t-shirt.
他穿着一件写着“投票给佩德罗”的T恤。

78
00:03:07.730 --> 00:03:09.070
Oh, Napoleon Dynamite fan.
噢，是《拿破仑炸药》的粉丝。

79
00:03:09.070 --> 00:03:09.430
Yes.
是的。

80
00:03:09.550 --> 00:03:09.770
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

81
00:03:09.850 --> 00:03:10.250
Yes.
没错。

82
00:03:10.510 --> 00:03:11.770
We check my bumper.
我们检查了我的保险杠。

83
00:03:12.570 --> 00:03:14.230
Nothing to write home about.
没什么大碍。

84
00:03:14.410 --> 00:03:15.450
We're all going to be fine.
我们都没事。

85
00:03:15.690 --> 00:03:17.030
But here's the kicker.
但重点来了。

86
00:03:17.410 --> 00:03:19.910
Guess where he was going to go to work?
你猜他要去哪儿上班？

87
00:03:20.050 --> 00:03:20.410
Where?
去哪儿？

88
00:03:20.410 --> 00:03:23.110
The Wizarding World of Harry Potter.
哈利波特的魔法世界。

89
00:03:23.490 --> 00:03:24.970
Oh, at Universal.
噢，在环球影城那个。

90
00:03:25.310 --> 00:03:25.590
Yes.
对。

91
00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:28.530
Which we had just been to a few days ago.
我们几天前刚去过那里。

92
00:03:28.690 --> 00:03:30.910
And I got so excited.
我当时特别兴奋。

93
00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:33.090
I was like, oh, my gosh.
我说，天哪。

94
00:03:33.390 --> 00:03:35.410
He had just moved here from Hawaii.
他刚从夏威夷搬到这儿。

95
00:03:35.730 --> 00:03:43.470
He had borrowed this car from the person he's living with to drive to his job at Wizarding World of Harry Potter.
他借了室友的车，正要去哈利波特的魔法世界上班。

96
00:03:43.750 --> 00:03:47.090
You know, they all talk in accents in the Wizarding World of Harry Potter.
你知道，在哈利波特的魔法世界里，他们说话都带着口音。

97
00:03:47.350 --> 00:03:49.430
It's very theatrical, the whole experience.
整个体验非常有戏剧感。

98
00:03:49.970 --> 00:03:53.650
And I said to him, do they make you speak in accents?
我问他，他们要求你们用口音说话吗？

99
00:03:54.030 --> 00:03:54.290
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

100
00:03:54.290 --> 00:03:55.130
And he said, no.
他说，没有。

101
00:03:55.310 --> 00:03:57.410
If you have an accent, you can speak in it.
如果你有口音，你可以直接用口音说。

102
00:03:57.510 --> 00:04:03.170
But he said he does it anyway because he's an aspiring actor and he likes to do voice work.
但他还是说他会那么做，因为他是个有抱负的演员，喜欢做配音工作。

103
00:04:03.530 --> 00:04:06.250
We had a lovely chat on the side of the road.
我们在路边聊得很开心。

104
00:04:06.670 --> 00:04:08.050
And now here I am.
然后我就到这儿了。

105
00:04:08.570 --> 00:04:11.510
And he's in the lobby and he's going to – no, I'm kidding.
他现在就在大厅里，他打算——不，我开玩笑的。

106
00:04:11.510 --> 00:04:17.050
Like, I love the idea that he bumped into Pam from the office and you were excited about his job.
比如，我很喜欢这个点子，你偶遇了《办公室》里的帕姆，而且你对他的工作很感兴趣。

107
00:04:17.210 --> 00:04:17.650
I was.
我是挺感兴趣的。

108
00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:19.130
I was like, tell me everything.
我当时就像是，快把一切都告诉我。

109
00:04:20.270 --> 00:04:23.490
No, he did end up recognizing me and I took a photo with him.
不，他最后确实认出我了，我还和他合了影。

110
00:04:23.550 --> 00:04:29.390
So, if you know this guy and he tags us, I'll try to find it.
所以，如果你认识这个人，而且他标记了我们，我会试着找找看。

111
00:04:29.470 --> 00:04:30.270
I'll repost it.
我会转发的。

112
00:04:31.090 --> 00:04:36.610
But I love that you were just chatting him up on the side of the road because I would have been there for all of that.
但我很喜欢你当时在路边和他搭讪，因为如果我在场，我肯定会全程参与。

113
00:04:37.070 --> 00:04:39.250
And then I would have been like, what are you doing today?
然后我就会问，你今天打算做什么？

114
00:04:39.870 --> 00:04:40.270
I know.
我知道。

115
00:04:40.270 --> 00:04:41.910
I was like, well, I should probably go.
我当时想，好吧，我大概该走了。

116
00:04:42.090 --> 00:04:42.870
I have to go to work.
我得去上班了。

117
00:04:43.070 --> 00:04:44.410
I have to drop my daughter off at camp.
我得送我女儿去夏令营。

118
00:04:44.410 --> 00:04:44.850
Exactly.
没错。

119
00:04:45.250 --> 00:04:47.330
But we're all fine and we're here.
但我们都很好，也平安到达了。

120
00:04:47.570 --> 00:04:49.650
I think I'm maybe good for the day.
我觉得我今天大概没问题了。

121
00:04:49.870 --> 00:04:49.970
You're good.
你没问题的。

122
00:04:50.090 --> 00:04:50.430
I don't know.
我不知道。

123
00:04:50.530 --> 00:04:51.050
Knock on wood.
敲敲木头（祈求好运）。

124
00:04:51.270 --> 00:04:51.690
Knock on wood.
敲敲木头。

125
00:04:52.170 --> 00:04:52.590
All right.
好吧。

126
00:04:52.990 --> 00:04:54.470
That was my morning tangent.
这就是我早上的题外话。

127
00:04:54.510 --> 00:04:55.690
Should we get started?
我们要开始了吗？

128
00:04:55.990 --> 00:04:56.890
Let's do it.
开始吧。

129
00:04:57.450 --> 00:05:01.850
This episode of Counseling was written by BJ Novak and directed by Jeffrey Blitz.
这一集《心理咨询》由BJ·诺瓦克编剧，杰弗里·布里茨执导。

130
00:05:02.170 --> 00:05:03.470
And here's your summary.
这是剧情梗概。

131
00:05:03.970 --> 00:05:07.930
As a punishment for spanking Luke in front of the entire office,
因为在整个办公室面前打了卢克的屁股作为惩罚，

132
00:05:08.210 --> 00:05:12.270
Michael must complete six hour-long counseling sessions with Toby.
迈克尔必须完成六次、每次一小时与托比的心理咨询。

133
00:05:13.630 --> 00:05:19.270
Dwight seeks a pretty woman-style revenge on a salesman who snubbed him at the Steamtown Mall.
德怀特对一个在蒸汽镇购物中心冷落他的推销员进行了“风月俏佳人”式的报复。

134
00:05:19.490 --> 00:05:22.630
And Pam scams her way into a new job title.
而帕姆通过欺骗手段获得了一个新的职位头衔。

135
00:05:23.090 --> 00:05:26.010
I mean, in this episode, I was like, Pam, who are you?
我是说，在这一集里，我当时想，帕姆，你到底是谁？

136
00:05:26.630 --> 00:05:32.650
You know, when this happened, it was sort of like one of those controversial character moments.
你知道，当这件事发生时，这有点像那种充满争议的角色时刻。

137
00:05:32.650 --> 00:05:35.090
We got a lot of messages about it.
我们收到了很多关于此的消息。

138
00:05:35.170 --> 00:05:36.530
And we also got mail.
我们还收到了信件。

139
00:05:36.710 --> 00:05:36.990
Oh.
哦。

140
00:05:37.030 --> 00:05:37.550
So I'll read it later.
所以我稍后再读。

141
00:05:37.710 --> 00:05:37.970
Okay.
好的。

142
00:05:39.070 --> 00:05:39.750
All right.
好吧。

143
00:05:39.950 --> 00:05:41.370
Fast fact number one.
冷知识第一条。

144
00:05:42.390 --> 00:05:45.950
I mentioned that Michael has to do these counseling sessions with Toby.
我提到迈克尔必须和托比进行这些心理咨询。

145
00:05:46.250 --> 00:05:46.390
Yeah.
是的。

146
00:05:46.410 --> 00:05:47.530
That's our A storyline.
这是我们的主线剧情。

147
00:05:48.430 --> 00:05:55.510
It's revealed at two minutes and 52 seconds that Toby has a degree in social work from Temple University.
在两分五十二秒时揭示了托比拥有天普大学的社会工作学位。

148
00:05:55.810 --> 00:05:56.930
I took a picture of it.
我拍了张照片。

149
00:05:57.070 --> 00:05:58.930
He's standing so proudly by it.
他站在那儿，显得非常自豪。

150
00:05:59.010 --> 00:05:59.850
And then it goes wonky.
然后画面就变得扭曲了。

151
00:06:00.610 --> 00:06:01.130
Yes.
是的。

152
00:06:01.390 --> 00:06:07.550
Well, the shot is only two seconds long, but a lot went into getting that diploma because it is a real diploma.
嗯，那个镜头只有两秒钟，但为了拿到那张毕业证花了不少心思，因为那是真的毕业证。

153
00:06:07.550 --> 00:06:09.490
From the actual university.
来自那所真实的大学。

154
00:06:09.870 --> 00:06:14.010
We got a letter from Raymond Betzner in Williamsburg, Virginia, that says this.
我们收到了弗吉尼亚州威廉斯堡的雷蒙德·贝茨纳寄来的一封信，上面是这样写的。

155
00:06:14.750 --> 00:06:22.610
I was the associate vice president for marketing and communications at Temple University in 2010 and helped get Toby his degree.
我曾在2010年担任天普大学市场营销与传播副校长，并帮助托比拿到了学位。

156
00:06:23.450 --> 00:06:25.170
The degree is real.
学位是真的。

157
00:06:25.490 --> 00:06:28.990
How can Toby be a graduate from Temple University?
托比怎么可能是天普大学的毕业生呢？

158
00:06:29.370 --> 00:06:33.370
Oh, well, lady, we got a bunch of mail about, like, when was this happening?
噢，好吧，女士，我们收到了很多邮件，都在问这事儿是什么时候发生的？

159
00:06:33.590 --> 00:06:36.170
Was this before or after he was in the seminary?
是在他去神学院之前还是之后？

160
00:06:36.330 --> 00:06:38.790
Was it before or after he worked in advertising?
是在他做广告工作之前还是之后？

161
00:06:39.090 --> 00:06:41.130
Toby's backstory is much like Andy's.
