Well, we learned a lot of things we didn't think we were going to learn about Canberra.
嗯，我们了解到了很多关于堪培拉的知识，这些是我们之前没想到的。

315
00:14:04.340 --> 00:14:10.920
Yes, we still are unsure about the tunnels, but I'll tell you what, this episode of Mom Detectives just got more fun.
是的，虽然我们对那些隧道还不确定，但我跟你说，这集《妈妈侦探》变得更有意思了。

316
00:14:11.020 --> 00:14:11.920
Just got real interesting.
变得更有趣了。

317
00:14:11.920 --> 00:14:15.580
I mean, there's a lot that the Mom Detectives are going to see when we go there.
我是说，等我们去那里的时候，妈妈侦探们会看到很多东西。

318
00:14:15.860 --> 00:14:17.000
They're going to stumble across.
她们会偶然发现一些东西。

319
00:14:17.960 --> 00:14:18.360
Wowzer.
哇哦。

320
00:14:19.420 --> 00:14:20.000
All right.
好的。

321
00:14:20.160 --> 00:14:21.200
Thank you, Mika.
谢谢你，Mika。

322
00:14:21.580 --> 00:14:21.940
Yeah.
嗯。

323
00:14:22.620 --> 00:14:24.840
Let's move to fast fact number three.
让我们进入第三个速览事实。

324
00:14:25.180 --> 00:14:27.500
It's just a little location breakdown.
这只是一个小小的地点介绍。

325
00:14:27.500 --> 00:14:33.040
Our final storyline of this episode is going to have Dwight going to the Steamtown Mall.
本集的最后一条故事线是德怀特去蒸汽镇购物中心。

326
00:14:34.000 --> 00:14:38.300
We went to the Burbank Town Center Mall to shoot this.
我们是在伯班克市中心购物中心拍摄的这一段。

327
00:14:38.300 --> 00:14:46.180
And that precious heirloom store, that was created from scratch by our set decorating crew headed by Steve Rothstein.
那个珍贵的传家宝商店，是由Steve Rothstein领导的布景装饰团队从零开始搭建的。

328
00:14:46.340 --> 00:14:49.500
They used an empty store space on the second floor.
他们利用了二楼的一个空店面。

329
00:14:50.620 --> 00:14:59.580
And Randy shared with me that the original outline for this episode, like it never even made it into a script, originally had some scenes in a food court.
Randy跟我分享说，这一集的原始大纲，甚至都没写进剧本里，最初是有一些在美食广场的场景。

330
00:14:59.580 --> 00:15:04.080
And so, you know, they start prepping the episode long before we shoot it.
所以，你知道，他们在拍摄前很久就开始筹备这一集了。

331
00:15:04.080 --> 00:15:13.000
So, our locations manager, Kyle Alexander, actually had to find an empty store that we could dress that was also next to a food court.
因此，我们的外景经理Kyle Alexander实际上必须找到一个我们可以装修的空店面，而且还要在美食广场旁边。

332
00:15:13.480 --> 00:15:14.440
And he did it.
他做到了。

333
00:15:14.520 --> 00:15:17.320
We never used the food court, but pretty amazing.
我们虽然从没用过那个美食广场，但这真的很了不起。

334
00:15:17.860 --> 00:15:21.780
I mean, just another example of how they have to, like, always be ready.
我是说，这又是一个他们必须时刻准备着的例子。

335
00:15:22.020 --> 00:15:22.320
Yeah.
没错。

336
00:15:22.320 --> 00:15:25.180
And then maybe we didn't even need it.
而且也许我们根本就不需要它。

337
00:15:26.120 --> 00:15:27.440
They always hustled.
他们总是很拼。

338
00:15:28.180 --> 00:15:29.680
But, lady, that's all I got.
但是，女士，我能说的就这些了。

339
00:15:29.780 --> 00:15:30.880
Those are my fast facts.
这就是我的速览事实。

340
00:15:31.180 --> 00:15:34.120
Well, before we get into this episode, I have a little something.
嗯，在进入这一集之前，我有个小东西要分享。

341
00:15:34.460 --> 00:15:34.860
Yes?
什么？

342
00:15:35.080 --> 00:15:38.940
I wanted to share something from one of our office ladies' listeners.
我想分享一位《办公室女士》听众的内容。

343
00:15:39.120 --> 00:15:41.680
A lot of you might have heard of Elise Myers.
你们很多人可能听说过Elise Myers。

344
00:15:41.820 --> 00:15:46.060
And if you don't, go find her on Instagram or on the tickety-talk, as I call it.
如果没听说过，去Instagram或者我所谓的“滴答托克”上找她。

345
00:15:46.180 --> 00:15:49.260
I'm following Elise on Instagram, and I love her.
我在Instagram上关注了Elise，我很喜欢她。

346
00:15:49.380 --> 00:15:52.120
She is a delight and brings absolute joy to the world.
她是个开心果，给世界带来了绝对的快乐。

347
00:15:52.320 --> 00:15:52.600
Yeah.
是啊。

348
00:15:52.780 --> 00:15:54.100
And she's hilarious.
而且她非常搞笑。

349
00:15:54.680 --> 00:15:57.180
I mean, two words, Taco Bell, if you know, you know.
我是说，两个词：塔可钟，懂的都懂。

350
00:15:57.500 --> 00:15:58.780
That one went viral.
那个视频火了。

351
00:15:59.020 --> 00:16:02.140
But, you guys, she's also a fantastic singer.
但是，伙计们，她还是一位非常出色的歌手。

352
00:16:02.140 --> 00:16:10.840
And when I jokingly said on the podcast, can someone write a Whispers in the Breakroom song when we were talking about cover-up, she did it.
当我们在播客里聊到掩盖真相的话题时，我开玩笑说，有没有人能写一首《休息室里的私语》，结果她真的写了。

353
00:16:10.840 --> 00:16:12.860
It's awesome, and you got to hear it.
这首歌太棒了，你们一定要听听。

354
00:16:13.820 --> 00:16:18.040
I overheard that Kelly's Birkenberg is actually fake
我听说凯利的伯肯包其实是假的

355
00:16:18.040 --> 00:16:22.160
And that Michael can't remember his own middle name
还有迈克尔连自己的中间名都记不住

356
00:16:22.160 --> 00:16:26.280
And that Andy is always two hours late
还有安迪总是迟到两个小时

357
00:16:26.280 --> 00:16:29.500
These are the whispers in the breakroom
这些就是休息室里的私语

358
00:16:29.500 --> 00:16:34.700
I heard that Meredith turned her desk into a minibar
我听说梅雷迪思把她的办公桌变成了迷你吧

359
00:16:34.700 --> 00:16:38.780
And that Stanley schedules meetings and just sits in his car
还有斯坦利安排了会议却只是坐在自己的车里

360
00:16:38.780 --> 00:16:42.960
And that Ryan didn't graduate with a master's degree
还有瑞安根本没拿到硕士学位

361
00:16:42.960 --> 00:16:46.360
At least that's what I heard, but you didn't hear it from me
至少我是这么听说的，不过你们可别说是我说的

362
00:16:46.360 --> 00:16:51.360
These are the whispers in the breakroom
这些就是休息室里的私语

363
00:16:51.360 --> 00:16:55.740
If you want to know what's going on and you want it to come to you
如果你想知道发生了什么，又想让消息主动找上门

364
00:16:55.740 --> 00:16:59.780
The whispers in the breakroom
那就听听休息室里的私语

365
00:16:59.780 --> 00:17:04.780
Just stick around long enough and learn a thing or two
只要待得够久，你总能学到一两件事

366
00:17:05.940 --> 00:17:07.600
And that was Whispers in the Breakroom.
以上就是《休息室里的私语》。

367
00:17:07.720 --> 00:17:08.880
Back to you, Angela and Jenna
回到你们那里，安吉拉和珍娜

368
00:17:10.280 --> 00:17:11.540
Is that amazing?
这难道不棒吗？

369
00:17:11.940 --> 00:17:12.380
Amazing.
太棒了。

370
00:17:13.420 --> 00:17:15.140
I love it so much
我太喜欢了

371
00:17:15.140 --> 00:17:18.020
When I saw that, you know, I follow her on Instagram
当我看到那个视频时，你知道的，我在Instagram上关注了她

372
00:17:18.020 --> 00:17:20.380
And when I saw that, I was like, oh my god
当我看到的时候，我心想，天哪

373
00:17:20.380 --> 00:17:22.120
And you texted me
然后你就给我发了短信

374
00:17:22.120 --> 00:17:24.380
It was like a simultaneous thing
就像是同时发生的一样

375
00:17:24.380 --> 00:17:26.360
Where we were like, oh my gosh, we're seeing this
我们当时都觉得，天哪，我们看到了这个

376
00:17:26.860 --> 00:17:29.040
Elise, I love so much about that song
伊莉丝，那首歌里有很多我喜欢的地方

377
00:17:29.040 --> 00:17:32.680
It also kind of reminded me of when like Dolly Parton would harmonize
它还让我想起了多莉·帕顿的和声

378
00:17:32.680 --> 00:17:35.180
With Emmylou Harris and Linda Ronstadt
与艾美萝·哈里斯和琳达·朗丝黛合作的那种

379
00:17:35.180 --> 00:17:36.780
But you're doing it all with yourself
但你是一个人完成了所有的和声

380
00:17:36.780 --> 00:17:40.020
It's like my brain doesn't even understand how you do it
我的大脑甚至无法理解你是怎么做到的

381
00:17:40.020 --> 00:17:40.760
And it's amazing
这真是太神奇了

382
00:17:40.760 --> 00:17:43.860
Thank you for letting us play that on Office Ladies, Elise
谢谢你让我们在《办公室女士》节目里播放这首歌，伊莉丝

383
00:17:43.860 --> 00:17:47.600
All right, on that delightful note, let's take a break
好了，带着这份愉悦的心情，我们先休息一下

384
00:17:47.600 --> 00:17:50.520
Because when we come back, Jim and Pam are late to work
因为回来之后，吉姆和帕姆就要上班迟到了

385
00:17:50.520 --> 00:18:01.510
Well, we are back and Dwight is
好了，我们回来了，德怀特正在

386
00:18:01.510 --> 00:18:04.390
He's shaming Jim and Pam because they're late again
他正在羞辱吉姆和帕姆，因为他们又迟到了

387
00:18:04.390 --> 00:18:05.750
But you know what?
但你知道吗？

388
00:18:06.270 --> 00:18:10.230
You know, because Jim had to open that bathroom door a while back
你知道，因为吉姆之前不得不去开那扇洗手间的门

389
00:18:10.230 --> 00:18:14.210
They didn't get into the daycare that's close to Dunder Mifflin
他们没能进到邓德·米夫林公司附近的那家托儿所

390
00:18:14.210 --> 00:18:16.370
And now they have to drive all the way across town
现在他们不得不开车穿过整个城镇

391
00:18:17.070 --> 00:18:18.330
Dwight sees an opportunity
德怀特看到了机会

392
00:18:18.330 --> 00:18:19.770
He's like, hey, guess what?
他就像是说，嘿，你猜怎么着？

393
00:18:19.890 --> 00:18:23.290
There is a daycare center right here in this very building
就在这栋楼里就有一家托儿所

394
00:18:23.290 --> 00:18:26.070
Dwight is going to give Jim and Pam a whole tour
德怀特要带吉姆和帕姆参观一番

395
00:18:26.930 --> 00:18:31.370
Yes, the Sesame Avenue daycare for infants and toddlers
没错，就是芝麻街婴幼儿托儿所

396
00:18:31.370 --> 00:18:34.870
Where Mose has apparently been painting in the dark
莫斯显然一直在那里摸黑画画

397
00:18:34.870 --> 00:18:37.350
With a Cabbage Patch doll strapped to his chest
胸前还绑着一个卷心菜娃娃

398
00:18:37.350 --> 00:18:40.690
Is located in the former Michael Scott Paper Company
它就位于以前的迈克尔·斯科特造纸公司旧址

399
00:18:40.690 --> 00:18:43.930
Well, Jenna, I thought I would break down the special features
嗯，珍娜，我想我应该详细介绍一下

400
00:18:43.930 --> 00:18:46.910
Of the Sesame Avenue daycare center for infants and toddlers
芝麻街婴幼儿托儿所的特色功能

401
00:18:46.910 --> 00:18:50.690
According to Dwight, this is what your child's experience will include
根据德怀特的说法，这就是你孩子将要体验的内容

402
00:18:51.530 --> 00:18:54.590
A language skills and cognitive development area
一个语言技能和认知发展区

403
00:18:54.590 --> 00:18:58.050
Which is just an eye chart on the old rusty shower
其实就是贴在旧生锈淋浴间上的一张视力表

404
00:18:58.050 --> 00:19:03.810
There is one blue bouncy ball on an otherwise empty wire shelf
在一个空荡荡的金属架上放着一个蓝色弹力球

405
00:19:03.810 --> 00:19:07.910
A magical toy box that has plastic forks and knives
一个装有塑料叉子和刀子的神奇玩具箱

406
00:19:07.910 --> 00:19:09.710
And one soy sauce packet
还有一包酱油

407
00:19:09.710 --> 00:19:11.090
He was very embarrassed by that
他对此感到非常尴尬

408
00:19:11.090 --> 00:19:11.970
I know, he should be
我知道，他确实该感到尴尬

409
00:19:11.970 --> 00:19:12.430
He's apologized
他已经道歉了

410
00:19:12.430 --> 00:19:13.010
He should be
他确实该道歉

411
00:19:13.010 --> 00:19:15.550
There are four metal buckets
还有四个金属桶

412
00:19:15.550 --> 00:19:16.970
One is a restroom
一个是洗手间

413
00:19:16.970 --> 00:19:18.590
One is a feeding trough
一个是喂食槽

414
00:19:18.590 --> 00:19:20.210
One is a play bucket
一个是游戏桶

415
00:19:20.210 --> 00:19:22.210
And one is for a possible plant
还有一个是留着以后可能种植物用的

416
00:19:23.450 --> 00:19:26.290
And for those of you who love a good background catch
对于那些喜欢寻找背景细节的人

417
00:19:26.290 --> 00:19:28.130
If you go to 45 seconds
如果你看到45秒处

418
00:19:28.130 --> 00:19:31.130
The Cabbage Patch doll strapped to Mose's chest
绑在莫斯胸前的那个卷心菜娃娃

419
00:19:31.130 --> 00:19:32.970
Only has one red shoe on
只穿了一只红色的鞋子

420
00:19:32.970 --> 00:19:35.390
And the other foot just has a sock
另一只脚上只有一只袜子

421
00:19:36.430 --> 00:19:39.170
Did you have Cabbage Patch kids when you were younger?
你小时候有卷心菜娃娃吗？

422
00:19:39.890 --> 00:19:42.690
Oh, I was overseas and I came stateside
哦，我当时在国外，后来回到国内

423
00:19:42.690 --> 00:19:43.630
And everyone had one
每个人都有一个

424
00:19:43.630 --> 00:19:46.510
And I was like, I need this in my life
我就想，我的生活中也需要一个

425
00:19:46.510 --> 00:19:48.210
So yeah, I got one
所以是的，我买了一个

426
00:19:48.210 --> 00:19:49.330
What'd you name it?
你给它取了什么名字？

427
00:19:49.390 --> 00:19:50.150
I don't remember
我不记得了

428
00:19:50.150 --> 00:19:50.950
You don't remember?
你不记得了？

429
00:19:51.290 --> 00:19:52.610
This was such a big deal
这可是件大事啊

430
00:19:52.610 --> 00:19:54.130
I had two Cabbage Patch kids
我有两个卷心菜娃娃

431
00:19:54.130 --> 00:19:55.770
And I remember their names so clearly
而且我清楚地记得它们的名字

432
00:19:56.390 --> 00:19:59.050
Christine Marie and Casey Alexander
克里斯汀·玛丽和凯西·亚历山大

433
00:19:59.050 --> 00:20:01.730
Casey Alexander had curly auburn hair
凯西·亚历山大留着红褐色的卷发

434
00:20:01.730 --> 00:20:03.970
And Christine Marie had blonde ponytails
而克里斯汀·玛丽扎着金色的马尾辫

435
00:20:03.970 --> 00:20:06.450
Mine had blonde hair with some freckles
我的那个是金发，还有些雀斑

436
00:20:06.450 --> 00:20:08.170
I don't remember her name
我不记得她的名字了

437
00:20:08.710 --> 00:20:09.850
You didn't love her
你没爱过她

438
00:20:09.850 --> 00:20:10.990
I didn't love her
我确实没爱过她

439
00:20:10.990 --> 00:20:11.390
Clearly
显而易见

440
00:20:11.390 --> 00:20:13.030
I got her late in the game
我得到她的时候已经比较晚了

441
00:20:13.030 --> 00:20:15.070
And she clearly didn't make a stamp on me
显然她没给我留下什么深刻印象

442
00:20:15.070 --> 00:20:16.410
Oh, wow
哦，哇

443
00:20:17.350 --> 00:20:19.550
You remember I was trying to get Mandy Moore
你记得我曾试图让曼迪·摩尔

444
00:20:19.550 --> 00:20:21.290
To name her son Casey Alexander
给她的儿子取名为凯西·亚历山大吗

445
00:20:21.290 --> 00:20:23.910
In honor of my Cabbage Patch kid
为了纪念我的卷心菜娃娃

446
00:20:23.910 --> 00:20:25.570
I don't know why she didn't listen to you
我不知道她为什么没听你的建议

447
00:20:25.570 --> 00:20:27.210
Well, she has a second baby coming
嗯，她第二个孩子快出生了

448
00:20:27.210 --> 00:20:29.170
Maybe she'll take my advice this time
也许这次她会听我的建议

449
00:20:29.170 --> 00:20:31.290
Mandy, Casey Alexander
曼迪，凯西·亚历山大

450
00:20:31.290 --> 00:20:32.250
It's waiting for you
它在等着你呢

451
00:20:33.270 --> 00:20:34.530
Although, let's point out
不过，我们得指出

452
00:20:34.530 --> 00:20:36.710
None of your children are named Casey Alexander
你的孩子们没有一个叫凯西·亚历山大

453
00:20:37.730 --> 00:20:38.670
Well, listen
嗯，听着

454
00:20:38.670 --> 00:20:40.670
I had to ask Randy a question
我得问兰迪一个问题

455
00:20:40.670 --> 00:20:42.350
When I saw this cold open, Angela
安吉拉，当我看到这个开场戏时

456
00:20:42.350 --> 00:20:43.830
I needed to know
我需要知道

457
00:20:43.830 --> 00:20:46.250
Did they have to clean out this room again?
他们是不是又得把这个房间清理出来？

458
00:20:46.590 --> 00:20:47.610
Because it was storage
因为它本来是储藏室

459
00:20:47.610 --> 00:20:48.110
Yeah
是啊

460
00:20:48.110 --> 00:20:49.550
He said no
他说没有

461
00:20:49.550 --> 00:20:50.830
This is what he said
他是这么说的

462
00:20:50.830 --> 00:20:51.250
Quote
原话是

463
00:20:51.250 --> 00:20:52.890
We had finally gotten smarter
我们终于变聪明了

464
00:20:52.890 --> 00:20:54.130
And left the room empty
把房间空了出来

465
00:20:54.130 --> 00:20:55.450
And found a different place
找了个别的地方

466
00:20:55.450 --> 00:20:56.910
For post-production storage
作为后期制作的储藏室

467
00:20:56.910 --> 00:20:59.070
He was just so fed up
他当时真是受够了

468
00:20:59.070 --> 00:21:00.170
He was like, fine
他就像是说，行吧

469
00:21:01.250 --> 00:21:03.310
Randy also shared with me
兰迪还跟我分享说

470
00:21:03.310 --> 00:21:04.570
That Mike Schur
迈克·舒尔

471
00:21:04.570 --> 00:21:06.030
Who plays Moe's
也就是饰演莫斯的那位

472
00:21:06.030 --> 00:21:07.750
Was insanely busy
当时忙得不可开交

473
00:21:07.750 --> 00:21:08.830
